            <ArticleTitle>Interleukin-8 serum levels do not correlate with pelvic pain in patients with ovarian endometriomas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>450-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2009.03.074</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine whether interleukin-8 (IL-8) serum levels are correlated with pelvic pain in patients with ovarian endometriomas.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Prospective study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">Tertiary-care university hospital.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENT(S)" NlmCategory="METHODS">Interleukin-8 serum levels were prospectively analyzed in 51 patients (group A, asymptomatic patients or patients with mild dysmenorrhea; group B, severe dysmenorrhea and/or chronic pelvic pain and/or dyspareunia) who underwent surgery for cystic ovarian endometriosis to asses whether a correlation exists between IL-8 serum levels and pelvic pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION(S)" NlmCategory="METHODS">Interleukin-8 serum levels determination.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE(S)" NlmCategory="METHODS">Interleukin-8 serum levels and pelvic pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT(S)" NlmCategory="RESULTS">From 56 patients, five cases were ultimately excluded because the histologic diagnosis was not cystic ovarian endometriosis (2 teratomas and 3 haemorragic cysts). The mean (+/-SD) IL-8 serum levels in group A were 6.41 +/- 12.17 pg/mL and in group B were 6.52 +/- 8.73 pg/mL.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION(S)" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Pain symptoms in ovarian endometriosis is not correlated with IL-8 serum levels.</AbstractText>
